      "response": "- The number for the 1990 hotline for foreigners in Taiwan is provided under \"外來人士在臺生活諮詢服務熱線\" [1].\n- The services include consultation regarding visa, residency, work, education, culture, tax, health insurance, transportation, employment services, medical and health, personal safety, child-rearing, welfare services, legal information, and other life information [1].\n- Services are provided in Chinese, English, Japanese, Vietnamese, Indonesian, Thai, and Khmer [1].\n- Chinese, English, and Japanese services are available 24 hours a day, seven days a week [1].\n- Vietnamese, Indonesian, Thai, and Khmer services are available from 9 a.m. to 5 p.m., Monday to Friday (excluding national holidays and other rest days) [1].",
